          "text": "{\"evidence\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"p3\",\"quote\":\"There are uncertainties in the figures for mass and radius, and irregularities in the shape and density, with accuracy often depending on how close the object is to Earth or whether it has been visited by a probe.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p8\",\"quote\":\"many of the moons with a radius less than ≈100 km, such as Jupiter's Himalia, have far more uncertain masses.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p21\",\"quote\":\"That means that irregular bodies can have a longer chord in some directions, hence the mean radius averages out.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p21\",\"quote\":\"Radius is by mean geometric radius.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p30\",\"quote\":\"Radius estimated using equatorial radius and assuming body is spherical\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p31\",\"quote\":\"Radius has been determined by various methods, such as optical (Hubble), thermal (Spitzer), or direct imaging via spacecraft\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p44\",\"quote\":\"Radius estimated from an assumed albedo\"}]}"
